# CONTRIB-STATE - continual contribution mode (schema template)

The record half of the mode. The RULE lives in the control-plane skill; this
file records only the VALUE and its history. Append-only: rows are never
rewritten or removed, so every counter the gate reports is recomputed from
timestamps rather than remembered.

This template carries the fixed header and an empty state. It contains no live
rows. An installed copy is the operator's own runtime record, and a missing
record reads as `external_contrib: off`.

One flag, one home, fail closed:

- `internal_contrib` is the always-on half. The gate refuses `off` unless the
  same record cites `decision: <id>` for a recorded operator decision.
- `external_contrib` is the kill switch. An absent record, an unreadable
  record, or a value outside `{on, off}` all read as `off`: no remote write of
  any kind, including a push to a fork. A local branch, commit, test run, and
  rendered draft stay allowed.

Gate: `scripts/protean-ops/check-contrib-state.py` (G-14). Read-only,
stdlib-only, fail-closed.

## Header (fixed keys)

| key | value |
|---|---|
| schema_version | 1 |
| internal_contrib | on |
| external_contrib | off |
| read_at | - |
| mode_epoch | - |
| last_change | - |

- `read_at`: UTC when a dispatch last read the value, recorded together with the
  file's md5 in the lane receipt. A value read earlier in a lane is not
  authority.
- `mode_epoch`: the fingerprint of the last idle epoch claimed. One epoch is
  claimed once.
- `last_change`: UTC, actor, and reason of the last header change. A flip to
  `on` also appends a `switch` row that cites the operator reference.

## Rows (append-only; fixed columns)

| row id | kind | repo | action | thread | mode | authority | detail | lane / session | time | evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| (empty state - no rows recorded) | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - | - |

Column notes:

- `row id`: `cc-<UTC yyyymmdd-hhmmss>`, unique.
- `kind`: `epoch`, `switch`, `lane`, `submitted`, `grant`, `consumed`, `blocked`,
  or `note`.
- `repo`: `owner/name`, or `-`.
- `action`: `pr`, `issue`, `comment`, `review`, `merge`, or `-`.
- `thread`: the pull request or issue number, or `-`.
- `mode`: `internal` or `external`.
- `authority`: `internal-default`, `grant <id>`, `approval <ref>`, or `-`.
- `detail`: `key=value` tokens the gate reads. A `lane` row carries
  `lease_until=<UTC>`. A `grant` row carries `grant_id=`, `class=`, `scope=`,
  `expires=`, `max_actions=`, and the gates that must be green for each use. A
  `consumed` row names its grant in both `authority` and `detail`.
- `time`: UTC ISO-8601.
- `evidence`: the path to the raw command output that backs the row.

## What the gate enforces from this record

| rule | bounded value |
|---|---|
| live contribution lanes | 2 total, of which at most 1 external |
| external pull requests opened | 1 per 24 h (any repo), 3 per 7 d (any repo) |
| external issues opened | 1 per 24 h (any repo), 1 per 7 d (one repo) |
| external comments plus reviews | 2 per 24 h, 5 per 7 d |
| writes to one thread | 1 per 24 h |
| writes to one repo, any kind | 2 tolerated inside 1 h; the next is refused and the switch flips to off pending review |
| external write window | 05:00-21:00 in `America/New_York`, checked at write time |
| grant validity | `expires` within 14 days, `max_actions` at most 3, one consumption row per use, no expired grant |

Not derivable from this record, and therefore not claimed by this gate: live
repository backlog counts and thread attention metrics. A lane reads those live
and records the raw output in its own evidence file.
